Here is the full solution.

function countVowels(text) {
  const vowels = 'aeiou';
  let count = 0;
  for (const character of text.toLowerCase()) {
    if (vowels.includes(character)) {
      count += 1;
    }
  }
  return count;
}

Lowercasing first means one check covers capital and small letters, and `includes` asks whether the character is one of the vowels.
